Z            The mechanism used to produce "printf" style output  is
Z       the DDDDBBBBUUUUGGGG____NNNN macro, where NNNN is replaced by the matching number
Z       of arguments to the macro.  Unfortunately, the standard UUUUNNNNIIIIXXXX
Z       C preprocessor does not allow macros to have variable number
Z       of arguments.  If it did,  then  a  single  macro  (such  as
Z       DBUG_PRINTF) could replace all the DDDDBBBBUUUUGGGG____NNNN macros.
Z
Z
Z            To allow selection of output from specific macros,  the
Z       first  argument  to  every  DDDDBBBBUUUUGGGG____NNNN  macro is a _d_b_u_g keyword.
Z       When this keyword appears in the argument list  of  the  'd'
Z       flag    in    a    debug    control   string,   as   in   "-
Z       #d,keyword1,keyword2,...:t", output from  the  corresponding
Z       macro  is enabled.  The default when there is no 'd' flag in
Z       the control string is  to  enable  output  from  all  DDDDBBBBUUUUGGGG____NNNN
Z       macros.
